        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Cash Flow Statement - Following the Money",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The income statement is computed on accruals (file 05), so net income is *not* cash. The cash\nflow statement (CFS) exists to **reconcile accrual profit to the actual movement of cash**\nand to bucket that movement into three activities. Its bottom line is the change in the cash\nbalance — which must equal the difference between the cash line on this period's balance\nsheet and last period's. That tie-out is the articulation property that makes the three\nstatements one system."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-CASH-FLOW-STATEMENT.md#003",
      "path": [
        "04-CASH-FLOW-STATEMENT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:accounting:04-cash-flow-statement, git-history:accounting:04-cash-flow-statement]",
        "canonical_path": "accounting/04-CASH-FLOW-STATEMENT.md",
        "concepts": "[cash flow statement, operating activities, investing, financing, indirect method, free cash flow]",
        "current_path": "accounting/04-CASH-FLOW-STATEMENT.md",
        "id": "maxim:accounting:cash-flow-statement",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "accounting",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[cash flow statement]",
        "section": "accounting",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Cash Flow Statement - Following the Money",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              CASH FLOW STATEMENT  —  for a PERIOD                        |\n|                                                                          |\n|   +------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|   | OPERATING (CFO)   cash from running the core business            |  |\n|   |   Net income, +/- non-cash items, +/- working-capital changes    |  |\n|   +------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|                              +                                          |\n|   +------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|   | INVESTING (CFI)   cash for long-term assets                      |  |\n|   |   - capex, - acquisitions, + asset sales, +/- securities         |  |\n|   +------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|                              +                                          |\n|   +------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|   | FINANCING (CFF)   cash with capital providers                    |  |\n|   |   + borrow, - repay debt, + issue stock, - buybacks, - dividends |  |\n|   +------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|                              =                                          |\n|   NET CHANGE IN CASH                                                     |\n|   + Beginning cash                                                       |\n|   = Ending cash    <-- MUST equal the cash line on the balance sheet    |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-CASH-FLOW-STATEMENT.md#004",
      "path": [
        "04-CASH-FLOW-STATEMENT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
